# Components

- One Button, Input, Select, Textarea, Checkbox, Radio, Modal, Toast, Tooltip, Dropdown, Link per project. Variants are props, modifiers, or theme variants — not clone files.
- Forms, toasts, and tooltips are defined once and reused everywhere.
- Colors, spacing, radii, type — from tokens / CSS variables, not magic numbers in every block.
- New screen: find an existing component first. Do not copy-paste a card if Card already exists.
- States (hover, focus, disabled, loading, error) live on the component, not on each page.
- Do not make a “button” from `div` + onClick. Do not make a “link” from `button` without a URL.
- Icon without text — only inside a component with an accessible name.
- Visual: one thesis per product (`frontend-design`), motion — `antigravity-design-expert`. Primitives stay singular. Project tokens beat a skill accent. No “design without components”.
